index 4479b53..7392b4d 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,43 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Phone verification during sign-up
+
+Sign-up sends a six-digit SMS code using [Twilio Verify](https://www.twilio.com/docs/verify/api).
+Set the server environment variables listed in `.env.example` using your deployment's secret
+configuration. Configure the Verify service for **six-digit codes**, enable SMS delivery to
+your supported countries, and keep Fraud Guard and provider rate limits enabled. Missing
+credentials disable SMS sign-up with an error; no simulated codes are accepted.
+
+The same-origin `api/signup` endpoint stores a ten-minute phone challenge in the Astro session,
+limits resends to once per minute per session, and permits five code checks per challenge.
+It calls the existing external registration service only after Twilio approves the code.
+Use a shared Astro session store when deploying multiple instances. The external registration
+service is managed separately: it must also enforce phone verification if other clients can
+call it directly. This repository cannot change that service's registration policy or guarantee
+that it persists the forwarded `phoneNumber` field.
+
+Automatic SMS extraction uses [WebOTP](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/identity/web-apis/web-otp)
+on supported browsers over HTTPS, with `autocomplete="one-time-code"` and manual entry as
+fallbacks. Configure the Twilio SMS template to end with an origin-bound line for the actual
+sign-up hostname (without a scheme, port, or path), for example:
+
+```text
+Your DevTools Times verification code is 123456.
+
+@your-signup-host.example #123456
+```
+
+Both occurrences of `123456` must use the template's generated code variable, not a literal
+value. The hostname must match the page where the user requests the code. Code extraction
+fills the input; users still select “Verify and sign up” to submit it.
+
+Run the automated verification tests with Node 24 or newer:
+
+```sh
+node --test tests/signup.test.mjs
+pnpm run build
+```
+
+Tests mock SMS delivery and registration; they do not send messages or create accounts.
